_1138":1151,"_1140":-7,"_1141":-7},{"_1129":1142,"_1131":33,"_1132":1143,"_1134":1144,"_1136":1145,"_1138":1146,"_1140":-7,"_1141":-7},{"_1129":1130,"_1131":33,"_1132":1133,"_1134":1135,"_1136":1137,"_1138":1139,"_1140":-7,"_1141":-7},"key","document:skills/level-design/templates/review","kind","id","skills/level-design/templates/review","title","Level Review Template","description","Review a level's goals, spatial flow, readability, encounters, technical limits and next revisions using a reusable checklist.","url","/docs/skills/level-design/templates/review/","descriptionLanguage","originalTitle","document:skills/level-design/templates/playtest-report","skills/level-design/templates/playtest-report","Playtest Report Template","Record a playtest's task, observed behavior, participant comments, blockers and follow-up checks without mixing evidence and interpretation.","/docs/skills/level-design/templates/playtest-report/","document:skills/level-design/templates/level-brief","skills/level-design/templates/level-brief","Level Brief Template","Fill in a level brief with player intent, scope, routes, encounter goals, constraints and observable acceptance criteria.","/docs/skills/level-design/templates/level-brief/","document:skills/level-design/references/wayfinding-playtesting","skills/level-design/references/wayfinding-playtesting","Wayfinding, Player Understanding, and Playtesting","Test how players understand a space using observed routes, wayfinding cues and playtest evidence rather than designer assumptions.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/wayfinding-playtesting/","document:skills/level-design/references/tools-quake","skills/level-design/references/tools-quake","Tools, Resources, TrenchBroom, Quake, and File Formats","Review TrenchBroom, Quake workflows and level file formats with the tool and engine boundaries each requires.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/tools-quake/","document:skills/level-design/references/spatial-layout","skills/level-design/references/spatial-layout","Layout, Flow, Verticality, Critical Paths, and Gates","Shape critical paths, alternate routes, gates, verticality and flow around the choices a player should make.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/spatial-layout/","document:skills/level-design/references/source-map","skills/level-design/references/source-map","Source Map and Reading Coverage","Trace the level-design skill's topics and adaptations to the original Level Design Book reading coverage.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/source-map/","document:skills/level-design/references/scripting-doors","skills/level-design/references/scripting-doors","Scripting, Navigation, and Doors","Specify scripted interactions, navigation dependencies and door states with readable feedback and recoverable behavior.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/scripting-doors/","document:skills/level-design/references/optimization-release","skills/level-design/references/optimization-release","Optimization, Documentation, Packaging, and Release","Prepare a level for release through performance work, documentation, packaging and checks on the target build.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/optimization-release/","document:skills/level-design/references/lighting-art","skills/level-design/references/lighting-art","Lighting, Darkness, Environment Art, Texturing, and Storytelling","Use lighting, darkness, materials and environmental storytelling to support navigation, readability and the intended experience.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/lighting-art/","document:skills/level-design/references/learning","skills/level-design/references/learning","Learning, Teaching, Exercises, Critique, and Portfolios","Use exercises, critique, teaching methods and portfolio evidence to develop and explain level-design decisions.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/learning/","document:skills/level-design/references/foundations","skills/level-design/references/foundations","Foundations, Pre-production, Research, Worldbuilding, and Scope","Set player intent, research questions, worldbuilding constraints and project scope before drawing a level layout.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/foundations/","document:skills/level-design/references/culture-history","skills/level-design/references/culture-history","Level Design as Culture and Historical Practice","Place level-design practices in their cultural and historical context instead of treating familiar conventions as universal rules.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/culture-history/","document:skills/level-design/references/combat-balance","skills/level-design/references/combat-balance","Combat, Enemy Roles, Encounters, Cover, and Map Balance","Design encounters around enemy roles, sightlines, cover, movement and multiplayer balance, then test the resulting decisions.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/combat-balance/","document:skills/level-design/references/case-studies","skills/level-design/references/case-studies","Studying Levels and Transferring Their Relationships","Study existing levels by reconstructing spatial and gameplay relationships, then adapt those relationships to a new brief.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/case-studies/","document:skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics","skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics","Blockout, Massing, Landscape, Composition, and Metrics","Plan graybox massing, terrain, composition and player-scale metrics before committing to finished environment art.","/docs/skills/level-design/references/blockout-metrics/","document:editorial-art-prompts","editorial-art-prompts","GameMap editorial art prompts","Inspect the prompts and provenance for GameMap's AI-generated editorial artwork, separate from authentic project previews.","/docs/editorial-art-prompts/","document:design/v2/design-system","design/v2/design-system","Historical design archive · World Studio concept","Historical archive of the World Studio concept, preserving an earlier design iteration and its superseded build assumptions.","/docs/design/v2/design-system/","document:design/design-system","design/design-system","Historical design archive · first concept","Historical archive of GameMap's first visual concept; its palette, fonts and layout are superseded rather than current requirements.","/docs/design/design-system/","document:zh/publishing-platforms","zh/publishing-platforms","发现游戏，发布自己的作品","从官方入口了解 Steam、itch.io 等游戏平台，分清试玩、下载、源码与发行状态。","/docs/zh/publishing-platforms/","document:zh/deployment","zh/deployment","在本地运行和发布 GameMap","在本地启动 GameMap，了解源资料自动刷新、生产构建预览与 GitHub Pages 部署方式。","/docs/zh/deployment/","document:zh/level-design-skill","zh/level-design-skill","关卡设计 Skill","了解关卡设计 Skill 的适用范围、下载入口、简报与试玩模板，以及来源和非商业许可条件。","/docs/zh/level-design-skill/","document:zh/practical-guide","zh/practical-guide","从想法到可玩的游戏","用一个无需安装依赖的 HTML 小游戏跑通开始、游玩、胜负与重试，再完成一次边界明确的修改。","/docs/zh/practical-guide/","document:zh/reading-guide","zh/reading-guide","怎样使用这份资料库","按当前问题选择工具、案例或研究资料，分清来源、可运行性、许可与实际验证范围。","/docs/zh/reading-guide/","document:skills/level-design/LICENSE","skills/level-design/LICENSE","Attribution, License, and Adaptation Notice","Read attribution and CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 reuse conditions for the unofficial Level Design Book skill adaptation.","/docs/skills/level-design/LICENSE/","document:skills/level-design/SKILL","skills/level-design/SKILL","Level Design: From Intended Experience to Tested Space","Route a level-design task from player intent and research through layout, grayboxing, playtesting and revision.","/docs/skills/level-design/SKILL/","document:level-design-skill","level-design-skill","Level design skill","Use a source-attributed level-design skill package with topical references, brief and playtest templates, and clear license terms.","/docs/level-design-skill/","document:content-model","content-model","Content model and coverage contract","Understand registered content kinds, source ownership, localization, generated outputs and completeness checks.","/docs/content-model/","document:deployment","deployment","Website development and deployment","Run GameMap locally with automatic source refresh, verify a static build and publish it through GitHub Pages.","/docs/deployment/","document:icon-sources","icon-sources","GameMap resource logo sources","Find the official sources, local files and attribution records for resource logos and visual identity assets.","/docs/icon-sources/","document:media-sources","media-sources","GameMap demo media sources","Trace project previews and recordings to their original creators, capture methods, credits and reuse limitations.","/docs/media-sources/","document:contributing","contributing","Contributing to GameMap","Contribute resources and game cases with primary evidence, accurate source scope, runnable access and clear attribution.","/docs/contributing/","document:catalog","catalog","Awesome AI Game Development","Browse the complete resource catalog with categories, source links and scope notes for AI-assisted game development.","/docs/catalog/","document:overview","overview","GameMap","Explore GameMap, an OpenEnvision project connecting AI game-development tools, playable projects and practical production knowledge.","/docs/overview/","document:community-case-research","community-case-research","Community AI game case review","Inspect the research log behind community game cases, including source completeness, AI attribution, play checks and rejected candidates.","/docs/community-case-research/","document:source-revision-notes","source-revision-notes","Source revision and implementation boundaries","Trace research claims to reviewed source revisions and distinguish stable release evidence from moving documentation.","/docs/source-revision-notes/","document:catalog-review-coverage","catalog-review-coverage","Catalog review coverage","Read the catalog's source-review ledger, including verification scope, rejected claims and remaining coverage gaps.","/docs/catalog-review-coverage/","document:agent-interface-evidence","agent-interface-evidence","Coding-agent game interfaces: source evidence","Review engine-agent interfaces for permissions, observations, reset behavior and evidence of the operations they actually expose.","/docs/agent-interface-evidence/","document:gameplay-state-contracts","gameplay-state-contracts","Gameplay state, narrative checkpoints and durable effects","Specify durable gameplay state across saves, retries, narrative transitions, cancellation and restored world effects.","/docs/gameplay-state-contracts/","document:benchmark-reproducibility","benchmark-reproducibility","Reproducing game-development benchmarks","Audit game-agent benchmarks by environments, actions, resets, seeds, versions and the evidence needed to reproduce a result.","/docs/benchmark-reproducibility/","document:game-development-evaluation","game-development-evaluation","Additional evaluation research for agents that create games","Choose evaluation tasks and metrics that distinguish code completion, game behavior, visual quality and player experience.","/docs/game-development-evaluation/","document:visual-feedback-mechanisms","visual-feedback-mechanisms","Visual-feedback mechanisms for game-creation harnesses","Design a visual feedback loop that joins observations, task context, proposed edits and checks without treating an image as proof of success.","/docs/visual-feedback-mechanisms/","document:visual-evidence-research","visual-evidence-research","Visual evidence and agent-harness research","Choose screenshot, segmentation, video and frame-readback evidence with explicit capture identity and observation limits.","/docs/visual-evidence-research/","document:asset-selection-feedback","asset-selection-feedback","Asset candidate selection and visual-feedback creation","Turn asset search and review into a bounded selection process with candidate identity, reasons, feedback and acceptance checks.","/docs/asset-selection-feedback/","document:asset-validation-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","Asset interchange and validation contracts","Validate sprites, tilemaps, meshes, rigs, collision, materials and audio against the runtime behavior each asset must support.","/docs/asset-validation-contracts/","document:generation-delivery-contracts","generation-delivery-contracts","Generation jobs, artifact delivery and asset acquisition","Track generated jobs and artifacts through retrieval, cancellation, provenance and delivery to an engine or content pipeline.","/docs/generation-delivery-contracts/","document:generative-api-boundaries","generative-api-boundaries","Generative API and model boundaries","Check authentication, job lifecycle, quotas, output access and usage conditions before integrating a generative service.","/docs/generative-api-boundaries/","document:generative-tools-research","generative-tools-research","Generative tools: additional source-reviewed research","Review generation tools by the assets they produce, their documented interfaces and the work still required for game integration.","/docs/generative-tools-research/","document:production-coverage-gaps","production-coverage-gaps","Production coverage and remaining work","See which production interfaces and evidence contracts are documented and which executable integrations remain unfinished.","/docs/production-coverage-gaps/","document:production-debugging-contracts","production-debugging-contracts","Production debugging and evidence contracts","Match profiler, GPU, physics, memory and build evidence to a specific failure and a repeatable diagnostic task.","/docs/production-debugging-contracts/","document:native-operation-details","native-operation-details","Native operation details and lifecycle boundaries","Look up native commands and lifecycle boundaries for import, rendering, input, audio, dialogue and browser captions.","/docs/native-operation-details/","document:studio-production-case-studies","studio-production-case-studies","Studio production case studies and acceptance lessons","Translate documented game-studio engineering accounts into proposed workflows while preserving each source's scope and limits.","/docs/studio-production-case-studies/","document:production-work-orders","production-work-orders","Production work orders: artifacts, recovery and acceptance","Adapt bounded production task templates for asset integration, navigation, multiplayer, builds and other engine workflows.","/docs/production-work-orders/","document:engine-operation-contracts","engine-operation-contracts","Engine operations: completion, recovery, and evidence","Define engine operations with explicit inputs, completion, failure, cancellation and persisted output instead of relying on tool success messages.","/docs/engine-operation-contracts/","document:production-research-notes","production-research-notes","Production tools and acceptance boundaries","Connect production-stage tools and interfaces to concrete artifacts, completion signals and the gaps that still need testing.","/docs/production-research-notes/","document:research-index","research-index","Production research dossiers","Navigate production research by task, from engine operations and asset delivery to state, debugging and evaluation evidence.","/docs/research-index/","document:world-model-notes","world-model-notes","Coding World Models: Categories, Selection, and Research Notes","Distinguish executable code worlds, hybrid renderers, neural simulation and generated 3D scenes, with release and hardware limits.","/docs/world-model-notes/","document:cadle-repositories","cadle-repositories","Cadle-like repository research import","Inspect a source-reviewed ledger of Cadle-related games, browser projects, engines and agent harnesses, including unresolved candidates.","/docs/cadle-repositories/","document:game-ai-notes","game-ai-notes","2D / 3D Game Development AI: Research Notes","Review AI contributions across 2D and 3D development, including executable interfaces, version limits and evaluation claims.","/docs/game-ai-notes/","document:engines-notes","engines-notes","Engines, rendering libraries, and content tools: sources and scope","Compare game engines, rendering libraries and content tools by runtime role, source status and integration needs.","/docs/engines-notes/","document:agents-notes","agents-notes","Coding agents and game tool integrations: source review notes","Separate coding models, agent clients, skills and engine interfaces before choosing a game-development workflow.","/docs/agents-notes/","document:publishing-platforms","publishing-platforms","Find games and publish your own","Compare official game-store entry points and distinguish browser play, downloads, source access and release status.","/docs/publishing-platforms/","document:game-testing-library","game-testing-library","Game testing library","Choose runnable games, agent environments and asset sets for a concrete test, with setup and license boundaries.","/docs/game-testing-library/","document:coding-agent-game-code","coding-agent-game-code","Coding agents × game development: code resources and game sources","Find coding-agent skills, engine bridges and implementation examples, with client, model and game-source attribution.","/docs/coding-agent-game-code/","document:tutorials-and-demos","tutorials-and-demos","AI game builds","Play creator-documented AI game projects and inspect their complete source, setup steps and development evidence.","/docs/tutorials-and-demos/","document:practical-guide","practical-guide","From Resource Map to Runnable Game","Build a complete 2D game loop in one HTML file, test win and retry, then plan your next AI-assisted change.","/docs/practical-guide/","collection:claude-community-use-cases","claude-community-use-cases","Claude community use cases","Discover creator demos and build accounts. This collection also includes films, tools, and experiments beyond games.","/examples/#collection-claude-community-use-cases","collection:open-source-ai-game-jam","open-source-ai-game-jam","Open Source AI Game Jam","Browse jam submissions using AI in code, assets, or gameplay. The jam name refers to AI tools; it does not guarantee every game publishes its source.","/examples/#collection-open-source-ai-game-jam","collection:awesome-ai-built-games","awesome-ai-built-games","Awesome AI-Built Games","A broader community list across action, racing, adventure, strategy, puzzles, and arcade games. Source availability varies by project.","/examples/#collection-awesome-ai-built-games","collection:astra-game-source-collection","astra-game-source-collection","Astra game-source collection","Discover genre-grouped games with playable builds, source links and creator evidence. Check individual creator records for the coding client, generation scope and runtime requirements.","/examples/#collection-astra-game-source-collection","collection:ai-browser-game-jams","ai-browser-game-jams","AI Browser Game Jam","Find short browser games and creator tool or asset disclosures across the recurring AI Browser Game Jam. Submission pages do not guarantee complete public game source.","/examples/#collection-ai-browser-game-jams","collection:vibe-jam-games","vibe-jam-games","Vibe Jam games","Browse browser games from a jam requiring predominantly AI-written code. Participant attribution and public source availability still need checking per game.","/examples/#collection-vibe-jam-games","demo:recording-holodeck","recording-holodeck","Holodeck · A room from a prompt","An author-published tour of a generated bohemian living room.","/showcase/recording-holodeck/","demo:recording-infinigen","recording-infinigen","Infinigen · Articulated assets","An official showcase of articulated assets created through procedural generation.","/showcase/recording-infinigen/","demo:recording-trellis","recording-trellis","TRELLIS · 3D asset generation","An official Microsoft Research showcase of generated 3D assets. Project materials are presented for academic and research use.","/showcase/recording-trellis/","demo:recording-opengame","recording-opengame","OpenGame · Hajimi Defense: The Tuna Crisis","An official OpenGame demo showing a generated pixel game in action.","/showcase/recording-opengame/","demo:recording-solarrenderer","recording-solarrenderer","SolarRenderer · Official film","Preview the official cyberpunk street scene, then watch the full film for more examples of structural control and generative rendering.","/showcase/recording-solarrenderer/","demo:solar-voxel","solar-voxel","SolarRenderer · Voxel world, reimagined","A simple voxel scene becomes a richly styled, moving world.","/showcase/solar-voxel/","demo:recording-streamrender-h3","recording-streamrender-h3","StreamRender-H3 · Engine → neural render","An official synchronized comparison of engine output on the left and streaming neural rendering on the right. Both views are shown in full.","/showcase/recording-streamrender-h3/","demo:streamrender-car","streamrender-car","StreamRender-H3 · Engine to neural render","Compare the engine input with its matching neural render, in sync.","/showcase/streamrender-car/","demo:gamefactory-ue5-rpg","gamefactory-ue5-rpg","3AGameFactory · Village quest","Run through a stylized village, collect treasure, and watch the quest progress.","/showcase/gamefactory-ue5-rpg/","demo:gamefactory-ue5-combat","gamefactory-ue5-combat","3AGameFactory · Courtyard combat","Close the distance, trade attacks, and watch health react in an Unreal Engine 5 game.","/showcase/gamefactory-ue5-combat/","demo:opengame-skirmish","opengame-skirmish","OpenGame · Space-station skirmish","Move, aim, and dodge in a generated top-down action game.","/showcase/opengame-skirmish/","demo:opengame-portal","opengame-portal","OpenGame · Portal runner","Jump, fight, and move through a generated pixel platformer.","/showcase/opengame-portal/","demo:recording-solarwm-overview","recording-solarwm-overview","SolarWM · Camera-controlled worlds","The official overview shows camera-controlled movement across generated snowy villages, landscapes, ruins, and other worlds.","/showcase/recording-solarwm-overview/","demo:recording-triposr-assets","recording-triposr-assets","TripoSR · Single-image 3D reconstruction","Compare five input images with the rotating reconstructed 3D objects in the official TripoSR teaser. The complete input and output rows remain visible.","/showcase/recording-triposr-assets/","demo:recording-hunyuan3d-assets","recording-hunyuan3d-assets","Hunyuan3D 2.0 · Generated textured assets","Author-published rotating examples of textured 3D characters produced with Hunyuan3D 2.0’s shape-and-texture pipeline.","/showcase/recording-hunyuan3d-assets/","demo:recording-sprite-forge","recording-sprite-forge","Agent Sprite Forge · Earlier 0.3 sprite workflow","An earlier 0.3 introduction shows the Ryo workflow from a still image through video animation to a keyed sprite strip.","/showcase/recording-sprite-forge/","demo:recording-autoue-workflow","recording-autoue-workflow","AutoUE · Unreal Engine generation workflow","The official demonstration follows an automated generation workflow inside the Unreal Engine editor.","/showcase/recording-autoue-workflow/","demo:recording-diamond-csgo","recording-diamond-csgo","DIAMOND · A diffusion model of CS:GO","An author-recorded keyboard-and-mouse session inside a diffusion world model trained on CS:GO footage.","/showcase/recording-diamond-csgo/","demo:recording-genie3-jetski","recording-genie3-jetski","Genie 3 · Festival-of-lights jetski","Google DeepMind records a controllable jetski world at night, with directional inputs shown over the generated water and lanterns.","/showcase/recording-genie3-jetski/","demo:recording-wonderworld-cathedral","recording-wonderworld-cathedral","WonderWorld · Extending a cathedral scene","The official split view shows a cathedral scene expanding as the user chooses new content and a camera direction.","/showcase/recording-wonderworld-cathedral/","demo:recording-video2game-garden","recording-video2game-garden","Video2Game · Interacting in a reconstructed garden","An official browser recording shows movement and a ball-shooting interaction in a garden reconstructed from video.","/showcase/recording-video2game-garden/","demo:recording-sakura-crossing","recording-sakura-crossing","Sakura Crossing · A walkable neighbourhood","Walk beside an animated railway crossing in a cel-shaded Japanese neighbourhood generated with a local Qwen model.","/showcase/recording-sakura-crossing/","demo:recording-pokemon-tactics","recording-pokemon-tactics","Pokemon Tactics · Isometric battle","Position a team and target attacks across a 2D-HD tactical battlefield rendered with Babylon.js.","/showcase/recording-pokemon-tactics/","demo:recording-marble-blue-diner","recording-marble-blue-diner","Marble · A blue diner in 3D","World Labs tours a generated blue diner, showing a persistent 3D interior created from a text prompt.","/showcase/recording-marble-blue-diner/","demo:recording-raccoon-heist","recording-raccoon-heist","Raccoon Heist · Loot after dark","Collect loot under sweeping flashlight patrols in a Claude-built Three.js backyard caper.","/showcase/recording-raccoon-heist/","demo:recording-castle-clash","recording-castle-clash","Castle Clash · Prototype battle","Recruit a squad and send animated Tiny Swords units toward the opposing castle.","/showcase/recording-castle-clash/","demo:recording-cwm-brain-cloud-harbor","recording-cwm-brain-cloud-harbor","Code World Model · Cloud-sea harbor","An official recording of a wind-skiff navigating a cloud-sea harbor, with movement controls visible.","/showcase/recording-cwm-brain-cloud-harbor/","demo:recording-agent-arcade-galaxy","recording-agent-arcade-galaxy","Agent Arcade · Galaxy Blaster","A Phaser space shooter plays in a transparent desktop overlay above an editor.","/showcase/recording-agent-arcade-galaxy/","demo:recording-moonlight-mayhem","recording-moonlight-mayhem","Moonlight & Mayhem · Museum heist","Rescue a raccoon crewmate while avoiding a moving security patrol in a Three.js museum.","/showcase/recording-moonlight-mayhem/","step:world/experience","world/experience","Build an experience","Choose a research demo or product prototype based on model licenses, compute costs, and real-time requirements. Keep reproducible configurations and documented limits.","/paths/world/#experience","step:world/consistency","world/consistency","Test consistency","Measure long-term drift, action response, object identity, and collisions. Distinguish project demonstrations, paper evaluations, and reproducible open implementations.","/paths/world/#consistency","step:world/rendering","world/rendering","Render the world","Pass structural conditions from the engine to a neural renderer. Check geometry, action alignment, temporal consistency, and inference latency separately.","/paths/world/#rendering","step:world/dynamics","world/dynamics","Code the dynamics","Explore programs that express state transitions and rewards, or agents that update the environment. Check long-term state, object persistence, and editing capabilities.","/paths/world/#dynamics","step:world/actions","world/actions","Connect actions","Define the action space and environment interface. Distinguish language commands, keyboard inputs, and camera paths so model controls match the intended interaction.","/paths/world/#actions","step:world/state","world/state","Define the state","Decide whether code, an explicit scene, or video latents represent the world. Evaluate editability, interpretability, and visual quality separately.","/paths/world/#state","path:world","world","Explore code world models","Define state and actions, connect rendering, and test what persists.","/paths/world/","step:3d/release","3d/release","Ship your world","Package for the target platform, trim unused assets, and verify loading. Record engine and plugin versions, hardware requirements, and reproduction steps.","/paths/3d/#release","step:3d/testing","3d/testing","Playtest & iterate","Test scene connectivity, character behavior, physics stability, and frame times in the engine. Evaluate generated results with task checks and visual evidence.","/paths/3d/#testing","step:3d/assets","3d/assets","Create the assets","After generating or finding models, check scale, topology, materials, rigs, and animation. Prepare assets that the engine can load and use reliably.","/paths/3d/#assets","step:3d/gameplay","3d/gameplay","Build the loop","Build movement, camera controls, collisions, and key interactions in a graybox level. Give the agent runtime state and errors as feedback while developing the gameplay.","/paths/3d/#gameplay","step:3d/engine","3d/engine","Choose an engine","Choose the engine, renderer, and physics approach, then connect MCP or editor automation. Plan for both code changes and scene or asset operations in the editor.","/paths/3d/#engine","step:3d/scope","3d/scope","Plan & scope","Define the camera, character controls, core interactions, and target hardware. Start with one room or level to keep the scope of the 3D project manageable.","/paths/3d/#scope","path:3d","3d","Build a 3D game","Start with one space, establish a working loop, and prepare game-ready assets.","/paths/3d/","step:2d/release","2d/release","Build for the target platform and check asset paths, controls, and loading. Record dependency versions, generation prompts, and known limits for the next iteration.","/paths/2d/#release","step:2d/testing","2d/testing","Combine scripted inputs, state assertions, and key screenshots. Track build, gameplay, and visual issues separately, then playtest with people and adjust the pacing.","/paths/2d/#testing","step:2d/assets","2d/assets","Set the art direction, sprite dimensions, frame counts, and anchors before generating or finding assets. Check transparency, collision shapes, and animation states on import.","/paths/2d/#assets","step:2d/gameplay","2d/gameplay","Implement movement, interaction, scoring, and restart in small steps. Run the game and inspect screenshots after each change to build a playable loop.","/paths/2d/#gameplay","step:2d/engine","2d/engine","Choose an engine for your platform, programming language, and editing needs. Give the agent a fixed version, official APIs, and a working starting point.","/paths/2d/#engine","step:2d/scope","2d/scope","Define player actions, win and loss conditions, and the target platform. Keep the first version focused on one repeatable core loop.","/paths/2d/#scope","path:2d","2d","Build a 2D game","A small, repeatable path from a game brief to a distributable build.","/paths/2d/","testing-pack:asset-through-pipeline","asset-through-pipeline","Move an asset through the pipeline.","Kenney Animated Characters · Quaternius UAL · 100STYLE","/testing/#pack-asset-through-pipeline","testing-pack:give-an-agent-a-goal","give-an-agent-a-goal","Give an agent a goal.","MiniGrid · Crafter · ViZDoom","/testing/#pack-give-an-agent-a-goal","testing-pack:change-a-game","change-a-game","Change a working game.","Godot demos · SuperTux · Wesnoth","/testing/#pack-change-a-game","testing:mixamo","mixamo","Mixamo","A common ordinary game-animation workflow whose AI testing permission needs separate confirmation.","/testing/mixamo/","testing:smpl-model","smpl-model","SMPL-Model","A research representation for shape/pose conversion and human-to-game-skeleton pipelines.","/testing/smpl-model/","testing:smpl-body","smpl-body","SMPL-Body","The CC BY body subset for testing human mesh, rig, skinning and pose interchange.","/testing/smpl-body/","testing:amass","amass","AMASS","Research-scale human motion for pose pipelines and motion models in a common parameter space.","/testing/amass/","testing:lafan1","lafan1","LaFAN1","Research data and baselines for motion in-betweening, trajectory continuity and obstacle transitions.","/testing/lafan1/","testing:cmu-mocap","cmu-mocap","CMU Motion Capture Database","A broad motion source for skeleton parsing, coordinate conversion and control or retargeting research.","/testing/cmu-mocap/","testing:100style","100style","100STYLE","Styled locomotion data for motion matching, gait diversity and cross-skeleton retargeting.","/testing/100style/","testing:quaternius-ual","quaternius-ual","Quaternius Universal Animation Library","A practical CC0 baseline for humanoid retargeting, locomotion blending and root-motion tests.","/testing/quaternius-ual/","testing:kenney-animated-characters","kenney-animated-characters","Kenney Animated Characters","Small CC0 characters for first-pass skinning, animation playback and import regression checks.","/testing/kenney-animated-characters/","testing:unity-asset-store","unity-asset-store","Unity Asset Store","Package and import regression fixtures when provider rights and the permitted automation route are established.","/testing/unity-asset-store/","testing:fab","fab","Fab","Useful import test content when the exact listing, license and AI-use fields fit the intended task.","/testing/fab/","testing:open-game-art","open-game-art","OpenGameArt","Broad community coverage for 2D content tests, with licensing recorded separately for every item.","/testing/open-game-art/","testing:ambientcg","ambientcg","ambientCG","A CC0 source for texture-channel, terrain, lighting and material-resolution test fixtures.","/testing/ambientcg/","testing:poly-haven","poly-haven","Poly Haven","CC0 realistic assets for material, lighting, dependency and visual-domain regression tests.","/testing/poly-haven/","testing:quaternius","quaternius","Quaternius","CC0 models and characters for repeatable import, material, collision and animation tests.","/testing/quaternius/","testing:kenney","kenney","Kenney","A practical CC0 starting point for small test scenes, asset replacement, collision and UI regressions.","/testing/kenney/","testing:unity-ml-agents","unity-ml-agents","Unity ML-Agents","An official toolkit and example scenes for physics, visual control, cooperation and competition. It can expose custom Unity scenes to Python policies and automated tests.","/testing/unity-ml-agents/","testing:godot-rl-agents","godot-rl-agents","Godot RL Agents","Connects editable Godot games to Python agents. Useful for changing gameplay, exposing observations and evaluating NPC control in a scene you own.","/testing/godot-rl-agents/","testing:nethack-learning-environment","nethack-learning-environment","NetHack Learning Environment","A demanding roguelike interface for exploration, inventory, tactical choices and long-term planning. Use the maintained NetHack-LE organization rather than the archived Facebook repository.","/testing/nethack-learning-environment/","testing:vizdoom","vizdoom","ViZDoom","First-person environments for aiming, navigation, combat and memory, with programmable actions and scenario controls. The perspective is 3D; the renderer uses Doom-style technology.","/testing/vizdoom/","testing:craftax","craftax","Craftax","A survival and crafting environment with vectorized simulation. Useful for longer action dependencies and comparing pixel-based versus symbolic policies.","/testing/craftax/","testing:crafter","crafter","Crafter","A compact survival world combining exploration, health, gathering, construction and crafting. Achievement progress exposes different strengths of a playing agent.","/testing/crafter/","testing:minigrid","minigrid","MiniGrid / BabyAI","Small navigation and language-grounding tasks with keys, doors, objects and partial observations. A practical first baseline for repeatable planning tests.","/testing/minigrid/","testing:unreal-lyra","unreal-lyra","Unreal Engine Lyra Starter Game","An official multiplayer starter game for ability systems, input, game-feature plugins, character animation and larger engine integration tasks.","/testing/unreal-lyra/","testing:unity-boatattack","unity-boatattack","Unity BoatAttack","A complete boat-racing sample for buoyancy, waypoint AI, camera control, water rendering, shaders and asset-loading regression tests.","/testing/unity-boatattack/","testing:zero-k","zero-k","Zero-K","An RTS for resource planning, construction, unit control, terrain interaction and multi-unit tactical decisions, with editable Lua game logic.","/testing/zero-k/","testing:red-eclipse","red-eclipse","Red Eclipse","A first-person arena game for aim, navigation, parkour, bot scenarios, real-time map editing and native client/server changes.","/testing/red-eclipse/","testing:luanti-minetest-game","luanti-minetest-game","Luanti + Minetest Game","An editable voxel sandbox for first-person navigation, digging, placement, crafting and Lua entity, texture and world changes.","/testing/luanti-minetest-game/","testing:supertuxkart","supertuxkart","SuperTuxKart","A full racing game for visual steering, continuous control, physics regressions, tracks, karts and model/material pipeline tests.","/testing/supertuxkart/","testing:openttd","openttd","OpenTTD","A transport simulation for route and rail construction, economic planning, pathfinding, saves and multiplayer synchronization.","/testing/openttd/","testing:mindustry","mindustry","Mindustry","A logistics and defense game for production chains, construction, resource planning and client/server changes in a real game project.","/testing/mindustry/","testing:wesnoth","wesnoth","The Battle for Wesnoth","A turn-based tactics game with editable scenarios and scripting, suitable for pathfinding, tactical decisions, dialogue and rules changes.","/testing/wesnoth/","testing:ddnet","ddnet","DDraceNetwork (DDNet)","A cooperative platform game with grappling, precise movement, maps and replay support for input timing and multiplayer regression tasks.","/testing/ddnet/","testing:endless-sky","endless-sky","Endless Sky","A complete space game for navigation, combat, trading and long-horizon mission planning, with editable data and a plugin system.","/testing/endless-sky/","testing:supertux","supertux","SuperTux","A complete platform game for jump timing, collision, level editing and visual/input regression tasks in a substantial native codebase.","/testing/supertux/","testing:godot-demos","godot-demos","Godot official demos","Small, separate engine projects for character control, physics, navigation, networking, animation and import/export regression tests.","/testing/godot-demos/","agent:aider-pong-game-editing-transcript","aider-pong-game-editing-transcript","Aider: an official Pong build transcript with real code edits","Aider’s own example records building Pong and then changing paddle colors, size, and ball behavior. It exposes the actual edit blocks and applied Git commits, making the incremental coding workflow inspectable rather than presenting an unexplained final screenshot.","/agents/aider-pong-game-editing-transcript/","agent:gamedev-agent-skills-router","gamedev-agent-skills-router","GameDev Agent Skills: engine router and test/code recipes","A community skill library whose router detects the project’s engine and loads task-specific guidance. Beyond a directory of links, it contains the actual skill bodies, source-backed code recipes, a skill validator, and asset-report/preview utilities.","/agents/gamedev-agent-skills-router/","agent:playgama-web-game-assets-skill","playgama-web-game-assets-skill","Playgama: asset-production skill and GLB/audio build pipeline","A coding-agent skill for choosing a coherent asset set, recording credits, and preparing it for shipping. Its executable pipeline cleans and compresses GLB models while preserving names, handles audio conversion, and can re-encode textures.","/agents/playgama-web-game-assets-skill/","agent:playgama-web-game-performance-skill","playgama-web-game-performance-skill","Playgama: web-game performance skill and executable probes","A reusable skill that measures a running game after warm-up and guides performance fixes using frame time, JavaScript cost, draw calls, and triangles. It includes both a headless measurement script and an in-game probe for real-device observation.","/agents/playgama-web-game-performance-skill/","agent:godot-prompter-agent-skills","godot-prompter-agent-skills","GodotPrompter: multi-agent Godot skills and reusable movement code","A Godot-specific skill framework spanning gameplay, scene architecture, shaders, animation, testing, exports, and code review. It includes concrete GDScript/C# recipes, agent routing, platform-specific metadata, an OpenCode plugin, and machine-readable host verification status.","/agents/godot-prompter-agent-skills/","agent:phaser-official-agent-skills","phaser-official-agent-skills","Phaser 4: official coding-agent skills with engine code examples","The Phaser engine repository now provides subsystem skills for agent-assisted development, including scenes, Arcade/Matter physics, input, assets, cameras, animation, UI, and migration. The official README explicitly names several coding agents, and the skills contain practical API examples linked to engine source.","/agents/phaser-official-agent-skills/","agent:gemini-cli-godot-dock-bridge","gemini-cli-godot-dock-bridge","Gemini Assistant: a Godot dock backed by the actual Gemini CLI","A small community Godot editor plugin that sends prompts from a dock to a Python subprocess, invokes the installed gemini command, and handles returned file/folder creation instructions. Its code confirms a CLI integration rather than a direct Gemini API chat wrapper.","/agents/gemini-cli-godot-dock-bridge/","agent:summer-gemini-engine-extension","summer-gemini-engine-extension","Summer: Gemini CLI extension, engine MCP, and game skills","A publisher-maintained CLI/MCP integration for building scenes, writing scripts, playing games, reading errors, and taking screenshots in Summer Engine. It includes a genuine Gemini extension manifest, context file, skill packaging, and cross-agent setup code.","/agents/summer-gemini-engine-extension/","agent:gamecraft-bench","gamecraft-bench","GameCraft-Bench","An end-to-end game-generation benchmark with 140 tasks across 15 families, runnable Godot workspaces, replayable input traces, screen recording, and hidden visual/gameplay rubrics.","/agents/gamecraft-bench/","agent:gamelogicbench","gamelogicbench","GameLogicBench","A coding-agent benchmark of 72 gameplay-logic tasks whose deterministic Godot evaluators check observable state at each simulation tick rather than grading agent-written claims.","/agents/gamelogicbench/","agent:unreal-mcp-codex-runners","unreal-mcp-codex-runners","Unreal Engine MCP for Codex · Community Skill and Runners","A community Codex adaptation of Epic's Unreal MCP workflow, with concrete command-line helpers for environment probes, automation tests, Python commandlets, builds, and smoke cooks.","/agents/unreal-mcp-codex-runners/","agent:unity-agent-workflow-skills","unity-agent-workflow-skills","Unity Agent · CLI, Headless, MCP, and Package Skills","A reusable Unity workflow pack that routes agent work through CLI probes, batchmode validation, MCP selection, package management, and evidence-based completion checks.","/agents/unity-agent-workflow-skills/","agent:agent2unity-cli","agent2unity-cli","A .NET command-line client plus a C# Unity editor daemon that lets coding agents create and modify Unity assets through editor APIs and run compilation/test checks.","/agents/agent2unity-cli/","agent:godot-agent-loop","godot-agent-loop","Godot Agent Loop","A Godot build–run–observe–playtest–verify loop with runtime/editor bridge code, reusable skills, and retained execution evidence.","/agents/godot-agent-loop/","agent:gda-godot-agent","gda-godot-agent","gda · Godot Automation for AI Agents","A CLI, reusable skill, and MCP surface for editing Godot content, validating projects, and collecting runtime tree, input, screenshots, logs, and performance evidence.","/agents/gda-godot-agent/","agent:godot-cli-live-editor","godot-cli-live-editor","Godot CLI · live scene authoring for coding agents","A Go command-line client and embedded Godot editor bridge that let coding agents write scripts, construct scenes, connect signals, run checks, and inspect runtime screenshots.","/agents/godot-cli-live-editor/","agent:godot-forge-code-quality","godot-forge-code-quality","Godot Forge · code analysis and tests (gregario)","A focused MCP feedback layer for coding agents: Godot API lookup, GDScript and scene checks, actual editor diagnostics, and structured GUT/GdUnit4 test results.","/agents/godot-forge-code-quality/","agent:godot-forge-editor-bridge","godot-forge-editor-bridge","Godot Forge · live editor and runtime bridge (Tann2019)","An MCP server and Godot add-on for writing scripts, building editable scenes, reading diagnostics, running games, simulating input, and checking mechanics with saved scenarios.","/agents/godot-forge-editor-bridge/","agent:ione-unity-claude","ione-unity-claude","ione · Unity HTTP bridge and Claude Code skill","Connects Claude Code to Unity through an opt-in local HTTP bridge so the agent can inspect scenes, create C# scripts, wait for compilation, and verify the game view.","/agents/ione-unity-claude/","agent:tea-leaves-game-harness","tea-leaves-game-harness","Tea Leaves · Claude Code Godot verification harness","A reusable Godot project substrate that gives Claude Code runtime state, screenshots, simulated input, scene validation, and tests while it writes and repairs game code.","/agents/tea-leaves-game-harness/","agent:everything-game-dev-code","everything-game-dev-code","Everything Game Dev Code · multi-agent game workflow","A shared game-development workflow with engine-specific rules, coding-agent adapters, implementation and review commands, validation scripts, and complete sample game sources.","/agents/everything-game-dev-code/","agent:claude-code-game-studios","claude-code-game-studios","Claude Code Game Studios · implementation skills","A Claude Code skill and agent pack that turns game design stories into implementation tasks with architectural context, specialist programmers, review, and configurable completion gates.","/agents/claude-code-game-studios/","agent:codex-roblox-studio-bridge","codex-roblox-studio-bridge","Codex ↔ Roblox Studio bridge","A local Python server and Roblox Studio plugin let Codex create objects, change scripts, run Luau, and communicate through an in-editor chat panel.","/agents/codex-roblox-studio-bridge/","agent:gemini-cli-dinosaur-source","gemini-cli-dinosaur-source","Dinosaur Game Offline: a Gemini CLI-assisted source example","A small offline dinosaur runner whose creator explicitly describes Gemini CLI assistance with scaffolding, game logic, debugging, and improvements. It supplies concrete game code and committed images and sounds, with no generation API needed to play.","/agents/gemini-cli-dinosaur-source/","agent:phaser-game-agent-bridge","phaser-game-agent-bridge","Phaser Game Agent · Coding-Agent Bridge","Phaser's own setup CLI and stdio-to-HTTP bridge connect external coding agents to a managed Phaser game-building workspace, with a thin reusable skill.","/agents/phaser-game-agent-bridge/","agent:codex-game-studio-cli","codex-game-studio-cli","Codex Game Studio · local CLI and studio template","A Codex-native workflow CLI with tracked agent roles, reusable skills, engine reference packs, project state, task orchestration, and validation.","/agents/codex-game-studio-cli/","agent:epic-unreal-claude-skills","epic-unreal-claude-skills","Epic Games · Unreal Engine Skills for Claude Code","Epic's Claude Code plugin teaches agents to discover Unreal toolsets and operate a live editor through the native Unreal MCP surface, with a project-context session hook.","/agents/epic-unreal-claude-skills/","agent:gemini-cli-cloud-crush-source","gemini-cli-cloud-crush-source","Cloud Crush: Google’s Gemini CLI game source and codelab","Google publishes a complete match-3 game explicitly attributed to Gemini CLI, alongside a codelab covering plan mode, model steering, browser adaptation, testing, and subagents. The repository includes the resulting game rather than only instructions to generate one.","/agents/gemini-cli-cloud-crush-source/","agent:claude-game-toolkit","claude-game-toolkit","Claude Code Game Toolkit · Canvas engine and templates","Combines Claude game-development commands and domain skills with a small JavaScript engine, playable genre templates, and examples that can be inspected as real code.","/agents/claude-game-toolkit/","agent:codex-official-browser-game-workflow","codex-official-browser-game-workflow","Codex · official browser-game build and playtest workflow","OpenAI’s game-development workflow connects a written game plan, project instructions, generated assets, and live browser playtesting.","/agents/codex-official-browser-game-workflow/","agent:level-design-book-skill","level-design-book-skill","Level Design Book · unofficial design skill","An unofficial, agent-neutral adaptation of The Level Design Book for level briefs, blockouts, encounters, wayfinding, and evidence-based playtest reviews.","/agents/level-design-book-skill/","repository-research:Symbitic/awesome-babylonjs","Symbitic/awesome-babylonjs","A community-curated index of Babylon.js documentation, playgrounds, demos, scenes, games, examples, and tools.","/research/Symbitic/awesome-babylonjs/","repository-research:leereilly/games","leereilly/games","A historical catalog of GitHub-hosted games, engines, maps, addons, and related projects across platforms.","/research/leereilly/games/","repository-research:michelpereira/awesome-open-source-games","michelpereira/awesome-open-source-games","A curated catalog of source-available games, engines, maps, addons, and related resources across browser, native, and mobile platforms.","/research/michelpereira/awesome-open-source-games/","repository-research:slonce70/world-of-claudecraft-claude-bot","slonce70/world-of-claudecraft-claude-bot","A Node/WebSocket game bot with questing, combat, hea